notes.content:
We received a lot of Feedback regarding the annoying behavior of bots, so we had a serious talk with them about social distancing and some inconsequential attitudes. We made the following adjustments:


Bots now stop when they reach the character, no more kissing or hugging;
When low on health, bots retreat to seek healing;
Improved target system;
Bots can no longer use skills outside of players' field of vision.


Squad game mode is unfortunately not fun the way we expected, as well as the Bots are not acting as they should, that is, a little more strategic and less suicidal. We are revamping this game mode and soon it will be available again.

We've also implemented some improvements and fixed some bugs:

Improvements

The Gunslinger and Cyborg now have an ammo counter next to the character;
We've inserted a notice next to the "Quests" button when there are rewards to collect;
Being healed or taking damage from the environment now generates a healing/damage popup;
We've adjusted the colliders so that it's no longer possible for one character to completely block the other's path. 


Bugs fixed

Standard emote wheel equips the correct emotes;
Dash is now oriented towards mouse position, not movement;
The Cyborg bot was, in some cases, out of ammo for the entire game.


Planned improvements
We plan, in upcoming updates, to add visual and audible feedback when dealing damage to another character and improve the environment to add more strategic placements. We are also preparing two new characters.
We are closely following feedback from the community so you can continue to express your displeasures. You can send them to support@bullseyegamestudio.com

We wish you all a great game and see you in the next update!

- Hotkey Personalization
Players can now change the hotkeys for movement and skills. This option is now available under the Controls section on the options menu (in the lobby).

- New level system
The experience and level system is now balanced and following a fixed pattern. For older players, the experience gained since this patch will be converted to match the new level formula. The levels will be used to reward players on future patchs.

- UI improvements
LobbyRemoved the 'Online players' counter, since it was showing inaccurate data;
After pressing the 'Play' button, it will show the elapsed time, instead a regressive counter;
The experience meter on the player panel is now working properly.
IngamePlayer names now have different colors for allies (green) and enemies (red);
AOE skills color now follow the same pattern (green and red);

- Other changes and Bug fixSolo vs AI matches now reward half experience and gold;
Bots now have avatars, titles and names;
Fixed a bug where the Ninja chain was dealing 1 damage;
Fixed a bug where the Cyborg AOE skill was enduring 5 seconds instead 1.

For the next patchs, we're working on 2 new characters, Tutorials, Quests and more.

Enter our Discord Server to meet other players and have direct access to Developers.

- New party system

Now up to 4 players can form a party. You can invite your team mates by clicking on the '+' symbols on the lobby or directly from the frendlist.

- New UI features
 Brazilian Portuguese language support added;
 Minimap added;
 In game description of the skills (Tab key) added;
 Names of enemies and allies now have different collors;
 Language change option added to lobby;
 Small changes to the description of some skills.


- AI
 Bots of all heroes added;
 Behaviour of bots on squad mode improved.


- General
 Additional sound effects;
 Corrected bugs that could occur during matches.

Enter our Discord Server to meet other players and have direct access to Developers.
